{"strongs": "H2891", "word": "טָהֵר", "translit": "ta.her", "root": "טבר", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "be clean, pure", "definition": "טָהֵר verb be clean, pure (Arabic , id. ; Late Hebrew id. , Pi`el make or declare ceremonially clean ; Aramaic טְהַר emptiness , טִיהֲרָא brightness ; Sabean טהר Hal 682 ; Ethiopic purify, wash oneself with water ) — Qal Perfect ׳ ט Lev 11:32 + 12 t.; 3 feminine singular טָֽהֲרָה Lev 12:7 ; Lev 15:28 טָהֵ֑רָה Lev 12:8 etc., + 5 t. Perfect; Imperfect יִטְהַר Lev 15:13 ; Job 4:17 etc., + 9 t. Imperfect; Imperative טְהָ֑ר 2Kgs 5:10 ; 2Kgs 5:13 — 1. be clean , i.e. (miraculously) freed from leprosy by washing in the Jordan 2Kgs 5:10 ; 2Kgs 5:12 ; 2Kgs 5:13 ; 2Kgs 5:14 . 2. be clean ceremonially (only H P ), Lev 15:13 ; Lev 15:28 (twice in verse) ( P ), Lev 22:4 ( H ); by washing with water, the flesh Lev 22:7 ( H ); garments Lev 13:6 ; Lev 13:34 ; Lev 13:58 ; Num 31:24 (all P ); both flesh and garments Lev 17:5 ( H ), Lev 14:8 ; Lev 14:9 ; Lev 15:13 ; Num 19:19 (all P ); other articles Lev 11:32 ( P ); passing things through the fire Num 31:23 ( P ); offering sin-offerings Lev 12:7 ; Lev 12:8 ; Lev 14:20 ( P ); by the ceremony of the two birds Lev 14:53 ( P ); by ashes of red heifer Num 19:12 (twice in verse) ( P ). 3. be clean morally , of people, made clean by ׳ י 's scattering clean water upon them Ezek 36:25 of Jerusalem, specifically made clean from idolatry, under figure of adultery Jer 13:27 also followed by מִן Ezek 24:13 (twice in verse) (purification by ׳ י ); made clean מִכָּלחַֿטּאֹתֵיכֶם Lev 16:30 ( P ; by the sin-offering of the atonement day); also of the individual, be clean מֵחַטָּאוֺת Prov 20:9 (|| זכה ); become clean by use of hyssop Ps 51:9 (|| אַלְבִּין ); more generally אִםמֵֿעשֵֹׁהוּ יִטְהַרגָּֿ֑בֶר Job 4:17 shall a man be more pure than his maker ? (|| יִצְדָּ֑ק ). Pi`el Perfect טִהַר Lev 13:3 + 4 t.; suffix טִהֲרוֺ Lev 13:6 + 5 t.; 2 masculine singular טִהַרְתָּ Num 8:6 ; Num 8:15 etc. + 7 t. Perfect; Imperfect ; יְטַהֵר 2Chr 34:5 etc. + 4 t. Imperfect; Imperative suffix טַהֲרֵנִי Ps 51:4 Infinitive construct טַהֵר Ezek 39:12 + 5 t.; suffix טַהֲרִי Ezek 36:33 etc. + 4 t. Infinitive; Participle מְטַחֵר Lev 14:11 ; Mal 3:3 — chiefly P ; 1. cleanse, purify: \\ \\ a. physically , metals from dross Mal 3:3 land from corpses Ezek 39:12 ; Ezek 39:14 ; Ezek 39:16 heavens from clouds Job 37:21 temple from unclean things 2Chr 29:15 ; 2Chr 29:16 ; 2Chr 29:18 land and city from Asherim and images 2Chr 34:3 ; 2Chr 34:5 ; 2Chr 34:8 store-chambers of temple from household stuff Neh 13:9 priesthood by exclusion of alien blood Neh 13:30 . \\ \\ b. ceremonially , the altar of incense by the blood of the annual sin-offering Lev 16:19 ( P ); the people, gates, and wall (by some undefined ceremony) Neh 12:30 the altar of the court by the blood of sin-offerings Ezek 43:26 of consecration of Levites by מֵי חטאת Num 8:6 ; Num 8:7 ( P ), and חטאת Num 8:15 ; Num 8:21 ( P ). \\ \\ c. morally Lev 16:30 ( P ), Ezek 37:23 ; Mal 3:3 מֵחַטָּאֹת Ps 51:4 מֵעונ(ותׅ Jer 33:8 ; Ezek 36:33 מִטּמא(ו)ת Ezek 24:13 ; Ezek 36:25 . 2. pronounce clean , ceremonially Lev 13:6 ; Lev 13:13 ; Lev 13:17 ; Lev 13:23 ; Lev 12:28 ; Lev 13:34 ; Lev 13:37 ; Lev 13:59 ; Lev 14:7 ; Lev 14:48 (all P ). 3. perform the ceremony of cleansing Lev 14:11 ( P ). Pu`al Perfect 3 masculine singular טֹהַר 1Sam 20:26 (so. read for ᵑ0 טהור ᵐ5 We Dr , he is not clean, because he hath not been cleansed ); Participle אֶרֶץ לֹא מְטֹהָרָה a land not cleansed Ezek 22:24 (but ᵐ5 Hi Ew Co SS read a land not rained upon , see מטר ). Hithpa`el Perfect 3 plural הִטָּֽהֲרוּ Ezra 6:20 הִטֶּהָ֑רוּ ( Kö i. 271 ) 2Chr 30:18 ; Num 8:7 1 plural הִטַּהַרְנוּ Josh 22:17 Imperfect יִטָּֽהֲרוּ Neh 12:30 Imperative הִטָּֽהֲרוּ Gen 35:2 Participle מִטַּהֵר Lev 14:7 + 11 t.; plural מִטַּהֲרִים Neh 13:22 ; Isa 66:17 — reflexive: 1. purify oneself: \\ \\ a. ceremonially, especially in preparation for sacred duties Gen 35:2 ( R ), Num 8:7 ; 2Chr 30:18 ; Ezra 6:20 ; Neh 13:22 also for heathen mysteries Isa 66:17 of purifying priests, people, and wall Neh 12:30 (compare Pi`el 1 b ). \\ \\ b. morally Josh 22:17 ( P ). 2. present oneself for purification , only participle הַמִּטַּהֵר the candidate for purification Lev 14:4 ; Lev 14:7 ; Lev 14:8 ; Lev 14:11 ; Lev 14:14 ; Lev 14:17 ; Lev 14:18 ; Lev 14:19 ; Lev 14:25 ; Lev 14:28 ; Lev 14:29 ; Lev 14:31 ( P ).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3299')\">BDB3299</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H2891')\">H2891</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3298')\">BDB3298</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3300')\">BDB3300</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>טָהֵר</bdbheb> <b>verb</b> <highlightword>be clean, pure</highlightword> (Arabic <placeholder2067/>, <placeholder2068/> <highlight>id.</highlight>; Late Hebrew <highlight>id.</highlight>, Pi`el <highlight>make</highlight> or <highlight>declare ceremonially clean</highlight>; Aramaic <bdbarc>טְהַר</bdbarc> <highlight>emptiness</highlight>, <bdbheb>טִיהֲרָא</bdbheb> <highlight>brightness</highlight>; Sabean <bdbheb>טהר</bdbheb> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Hal')\">Hal<sup>682</sup></lookup>; Ethiopic <placeholder2069/> <highlight>purify, wash oneself with water</highlight>) — <div class=\"point\"><b>Qal</b> <highlight>Perfect</highlight> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ט</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Lev 11:32\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"32\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"32\" onclick=\"bcv(3,11,32)\">Lev 11:32</ref> + 12 t.; 3 feminine singular <bdbheb>טָֽהֲרָה</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Lev 12:7\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(3,12,7)\">Lev 12:7</ref>; <ref ref=\"Lev 15:28\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"28\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"28\" onclick=\"bcv(3,15,28)\">Lev 15:28</ref> <bdbheb>טָהֵ֑רָה</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Lev 12:8\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(3,12,8)\">Lev 12:8</ref> etc., + 5 t. <highlight>Perfect; Imperfect</highlight> <bdbheb>יִטְהַר</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Lev 15:13\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(3,15,13)\">Lev 15:13</ref>; <ref ref=\"Job 4:17\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(18,4,17)\">Job 4:17</ref> etc., + 9 t. <highlight>Imperfect; Imperative</highlight> <bdbheb>טְהָ֑ר</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"2Kgs 5:10\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(12,5,10)\">2Kgs 5:10</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Kgs 5:13\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(12,5,13)\">2Kgs 5:13</ref> — </div><div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> <highlight>be clean</highlight>, i.e. (miraculously) freed from leprosy by washing in the Jordan <ref ref=\"2Kgs 5:10\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(12,5,10)\">2Kgs 5:10</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Kgs 5:12\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(12,5,12)\">2Kgs 5:12</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Kgs 5:13\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(12,5,13)\">2Kgs 5:13</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Kgs 5:14\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(12,5,14)\">2Kgs 5:14</ref>. </div><div class=\"point\"><b>2.</b> <highlight>be clean ceremonially</highlight> (only <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('H')\"><reflink>H</reflink></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('P')\"><reflink>P</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"Lev 15:13\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(3,15,13)\">Lev 15:13</ref>; <ref ref=\"Lev 15:28\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"28\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"28\" onclick=\"bcv(3,15,28)\">Lev 15:28</ref> (twice in verse) (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('P')\"><reflink>P</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"Lev 22:4\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"22\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"22\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(3,22,4)\">Lev 22:4</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('H')\"><reflink>H</reflink></lookup>); by washing with water, the flesh <ref